test: normalize line endings before comparing the quoted prompt

A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes the READMEs as CRLF, and
test/docs.mjs searched for LF, so it reported "no quoted routing block found"
on a file that was perfectly fine. Normalize CRLF to LF before matching.

Adds .gitattributes pinning text files to LF in the repository so a checkout
cannot silently change what the docs test compares against. Re-verified that
the test still catches real drift after the change.
